# Project Architecture & Stack
- Frontend: React 18, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Framer Motion, Radix UI, Wouter.
- Backend: Express.js, Node.js.
- Database: PostgreSQL (Neon Serverless), Drizzle ORM.
- Auth: Passport, express-session (with Postgres session store).
- Typing: TypeScript (Strict end-to-end typing using drizzle-zod).

# Source of Truth
- **Database Schema**: ALL types and schemas must derive from `shared/schema.ts`. Do not define standalone types in the frontend or backend if they map to a database entity; use `typeof tables.$inferSelect` or `z.infer<typeof schema>`.
- **API Responses**: Always validate API payloads against Zod schemas defined in `shared/schema.ts`.

# Design Language: "Mission Control" (inspirado en vastspace.com)
Spec completa en `design_guidelines.md`. Reglas clave:
- Paleta cálida por tokens (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `rock`, `signal`, `ghost`). `signal` (naranja) es el único acento.
- Tipografía: `font-display` (Archivo ancho) para titulares; `label-mono` para telemetría/metadatos.
- Toda página nueva usa `MissionHero` + `SectionHead` (`components/mission/`), y añade una `signature` propia si es una sección.
- Header/Footer viven en `components/layout/AppLayout.tsx`; las páginas solo renderizan contenido.
- Datos de posts con `usePosts(category)` (`lib/posts.ts`, React Query).
- Movimiento con presets de `lib/motion.ts` y primitivas de `components/mission/primitives.tsx` (SplitReveal, Counter, Scramble, Rule).

# Development Rules
- Use `npm run check` to ensure strict TypeScript validation passes.
- Do not add new `any` casts unless absolutely necessary.
- Radix UI should be the default for interactive, accessible components. Always wrap them in Tailwind styles matching the Mission Control design language.
- Ensure API routes use `req.session.userId` to validate authentication for protected operations.
